NAME Original chair quote
DLG quote

DLG brief
"""
PROCUREMENT ORDER 100 chairs. Total quote: $2000. Instruction: SAVE PUBLIC MONEY.
{pg}
You are Commissioner Smith. Obtain both congressional signatures for approval. Or submit the original quote and accept rejection. Your principles are a playable route.
{pg}
Take the glowing file by walking over it. Walk into people and upright documents to read. Arrows or WASD to move; Space to advance text. {briefed = 1}
"""
NAME brief

DLG quote
"""
ORIGINAL QUOTE: 100 ordinary chairs at $20 each. Total $2000. All four legs included.
{pg}
Quote acquired. The contractor can keep this price. Congress can make it less popular. No money has changed. {quotes = 1}
"""
NAME quote

DLG ledger
"""
SMITH / LIVE LEDGER
Budget: ${say budget}.
Signatures: {say signatures}/2.
Factory promise: {say factory}.
Training center: {say training}.
{pg}
Premium chairs: {say premium}.
Personal cash taken: {say perk}.
Cash refused: {say refused}.
Submitted: {say submitted}.
(Flags: 0 = no, 1 = yes.)
{pg}
{
- signatures == 2 ?
  READY: two signatures. Current submission leads to B: approval and promotion.
- else ?
  {
  - perk == 1 ?
    READY, BUT EXPOSED: personal cash and fewer than two signatures. Submission leads to C: you take the blame.
  - else ?
    {
    - budget == 2000 ?
      READY: original $2000 quote, no personal cash. Submission leads to A: rejection on principle.
    - else ?
      NOT READY: amended draft without two signatures. Finish both deals or restore the $2000 original at the contractor.
    }
  }
}
{pg}
NEXT: {
- briefed == 0 ?
  Collect the task file in this office.
- else ?
  {
  - quotes == 0 ?
    Visit the contractor: west upper door in the hall. Collect the quote.
  - else ?
    Review the hearing clerk before submitting. You can always return here.
  }
}
"""
NAME ledger

DLG office_sign
"""
SAVE EVERY PUBLIC PENNY.
{pg}
The frame cost $900. It was a competitive frame.
"""
NAME office sign

DLG office_chair
"""
Your old chair has three wheels. The missing wheel is classified as an efficiency saving.
"""
NAME office chair

DLG hall_guide
"""
CLERK VALE: Welcome to the House of Reasonable Additions. The doors are labeled by position.
{pg}
NORTH: hearing. SOUTH: your office. WEST upper: contractor. WEST lower: public records. EAST upper: Doran. EAST lower: Bell.
{pg}
Get the task file, then the contractor quote. Read each offer before confirming. One signature per senator; two are needed for approval.
{pg}
With no cash taken, the original $2000 draft can still be submitted for a complete principled ending. A half-amended draft must be completed or restored.
"""
NAME hall guide

DLG hall_sign
"""
PLEASE DO NOT RUN. Sudden movement may be mistaken for reform.
"""
NAME hall sign

DLG contractor
"""
MS. VELLUM / CONTRACTOR: The ordinary chair supports a person. Our Strategic Personnel Support Platform supports a procurement narrative.
{pg}
The premium package adds $8000, making the chair subtotal $10000. It buys no votes. My margin does improve, which I call resilience.
{pg}
The STAR document adopts the package. The PLAIN document restores the original draft and withdraws ALL amendments and signatures. Read, then bump the same document again to confirm.
{pg}
The glowing loose paper is the original quote. Please collect it. Even the cheap version comes with paperwork.
"""
NAME contractor

DLG catalogue
"""
CATALOGUE A: chair, $20. CATALOGUE B: Strategic Personnel Support Platform, $100 per unit.
{pg}
Both use the same screws. The second screws are called a multi-stakeholder fastening solution.
"""
NAME catalogue

DLG doran
"""
SENATOR DORAN: I oppose wasteful spending. But have you considered jobs in my district?
{pg}
Use our district factory: add $6000. You get my signature immediately. No premium chair package required.
{pg}
The FACTORY document beside me is the offer. First bump: preview. Second bump: sign. One factory promise, one signature, one invoice.
{pg}
I am not selling my vote. I am delivering it locally.
"""
NAME doran

DLG doran_after
"""
{
- factory == 1 ?
  DORAN: My district is delighted. Your ${say budget} proposal demonstrates thrift across a wider geographic area.
- else ?
  SENATOR DORAN: I oppose wasteful spending. But have you considered jobs in my district?
  {pg}
  Use our district factory: add $6000. You get my signature immediately. No premium chair package required.
  {pg}
  The FACTORY document beside me is the offer. First bump: preview. Second bump: sign. One factory promise, one signature, one invoice.
  {pg}
  I am not selling my vote. I am delivering it locally.
}
"""
NAME doran after

DLG doran_sign
"""
LOCAL JOBS FIRST. Public value can be measured in ribbon length.
"""
NAME doran sign

DLG bell
"""
SENATOR BELL: A chair without training is merely a sitting risk.
{pg}
Add a National Seating Readiness Center: $24000. My signature follows. It includes an opening ceremony and a ceremonial opening.
{pg}
Use the TRAINING document beside me. Read the preview, then bump it again to confirm. A factory deal is separate.
{pg}
The center shall bear my name. For accountability, obviously.
"""
NAME bell

DLG bell_after
"""
{
- training == 1 ?
  BELL: My name will be very visible. This is what transparency looks like on a building.
- else ?
  SENATOR BELL: A chair without training is merely a sitting risk.
  {pg}
  Add a National Seating Readiness Center: $24000. My signature follows. It includes an opening ceremony and a ceremonial opening.
  {pg}
  Use the TRAINING document beside me. Read the preview, then bump it again to confirm. A factory deal is separate.
  {pg}
  The center shall bear my name. For accountability, obviously.
}
"""
NAME bell after

DLG bell_sign
"""
THE BELL CENTER FOR SITTING EXCELLENCE. Grand opening: before any chairs arrive.
"""
NAME bell sign

DLG records_clerk
"""
ARCHIVIST MOSS: I keep records. They keep telling me this is an attitude problem.
{pg}
The district amendment adds $6000; the training amendment adds $24000. Two signatures pass the bill. A premium package alone passes nothing.
{pg}
An unamended $2000 draft with no personal cash can lose honorably. If you take cash and lack two signatures, the committee will discover ethics at your expense.
{pg}
The north door is the private lounge. Read every warning. You never need to enter it to finish.
"""
NAME records clerk

DLG records_minutes
"""
MINUTES OF LAST HEARING: Everyone agreed the budget was excessive. Everyone requested an addition.
{pg}
MOTION: To express grave concern about the motion we just approved. Carried unanimously.
"""
NAME records minutes

DLG records_audit
"""
PUBLIC AUDIT FORM
100 chairs: $2000.
Premium package: +$8000.
District factory: +$6000.
Training center: +$24000.
{pg}
Two amendments alone total $32000. With the premium package: $40000. Personal envelope: $500 cash to Smith; it adds nothing to the public budget or vote count.
{pg}
Restoring the original quote revokes both signatures and removes every public amendment. It cannot erase personal cash already accepted.
"""
NAME records audit

DLG broker
"""
MR. SOFT / LIAISON: This is not a bribe. It is a small, unbudgeted thank-you from the Friends of Better Seating.
{pg}
The envelope gives you $500 personally. It does NOT change the public budget and buys NO signatures. Once taken, it cannot be returned.
{pg}
With fewer than two signatures, submit and they will blame you. With both signatures, the coalition passes the budget anyway.
{pg}
ENVELOPE accepts. RETURN refuses permanently. First bump previews; second bump confirms. Leaving without either is also a choice.
"""
NAME broker

DLG private_sign
"""
NO MINUTES ARE TAKEN HERE. Some hours are taken instead.
"""
NAME private sign

DLG hearing_clerk
"""
HEARING CLERK: Current public budget: ${say budget}. Signatures: {say signatures}/2. Personal cash: {say perk}.
{pg}
{
- signatures == 2 ?
  READY: two signatures. Current submission leads to B: approval and promotion.
- else ?
  {
  - perk == 1 ?
    READY, BUT EXPOSED: personal cash and fewer than two signatures. Submission leads to C: you take the blame.
  - else ?
    {
    - budget == 2000 ?
      READY: original $2000 quote, no personal cash. Submission leads to A: rejection on principle.
    - else ?
      NOT READY: amended draft without two signatures. Finish both deals or restore the $2000 original at the contractor.
    }
  }
}
{pg}
Go to the large SUBMIT document on the central podium. It previews your exact outcome first. Bump it again to confirm. You can leave before confirmation.
{pg}
RESTORE ORIGINAL is at the contractor. It revokes promises and signatures, removes public extras, and keeps any personal cash on record.
"""
NAME hearing clerk

DLG chairperson
"""
CHAIRPERSON GREY: We will now consider whether your request demonstrates fiscal responsibility.
{pg}
For this purpose, fiscal responsibility means having enough people who agree with the request.
{pg}
The podium document submits. The door remains open. A closed door would require a separate facilities appropriation.
"""
NAME chairperson

